    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **53 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## What I changed\n\n`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` \u2014 `getMembershipLevel()`:\n\nThe old code hardcoded `Math.min(level, 3)`, so level 4 was structurally unreachable and \"reserved for tenure\" only in a comment. I made tenure a real scoring factor and dropped the artificial cap:\n\n```\nlevel = 1\n      + 1 if email present\n      + 1 if namesakeCount == 0\n      + 1 if tenure > 365 days\n```\n\nI added a companion `getTenureDays()` = whole days from `registrationDate` to today (0 when no registration date, matching `getAgeBand`'s null-guard style).\n\n## Why this is correct\n\nThe tenure point is the **only** route to level 4. A newly created owner is registered today, so tenure is 0 \u2192 the fourth point is never earned \u2192 a new owner never exceeds level 3. This matches the spec exactly, including the illustrative case (email + namesake 0 + 3-member household \u2192 level 3, not 4).\n\nI verified the design against the existing tests rather than treating \"3-member household\" as a scoring factor \u2014 **Cp23** is the discriminator: a 3-member household with `namesakeCount` 0 and no email must be level 2. That only holds if household size does *not* contribute (1 + namesake0 = 2). The other tests (Cp15/Cp24/Cp39: email + namesake 0, zero tenure \u2192 3) confirm the pre-tenure ceiling.\n\nOne note: `getTenureDays()` uses `LocalDate.now()`, so an owner's level can rise over calendar time once their registration passes the 365-day mark \u2014 which is the intended \"tenure unlocks level 4\" behavior.",
